shopkeepers have nothing really interesting to say when you chat with them.
i think it would be neat if on occasion when you were lucky and appealing
that when you chatted with Ms. Manlobbi (or whomever) she would offer, for
a flat fee, to identify an item in her shop. of course, the shopkeeper
would only be knowledgeable about items related to her shop-type (i.e.
things she was interested in) and after awhile you may find yourself to be
less appealing and that the prices go up, etc. shopkeepers shouldn't know
about curses or blessings when identifying items. specialty stores might
charge more for information and less for items when compared to general
stores. also, dragging an army of pets into a shop should proportionally
decrease your appeal while in the shop. no pets gets +1 charisma while in
the shop. 1 pet gets no change in charisma, each additional pet gets -1
charisma while in the shop.

